{"seq":1,"prev_event":null,"at":"2026-11-21T00:53:28.898179Z","kind":"Started","body":{"audit":{"identity":{"mode":"t3-attributed","thread":"thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3Aff8efbf6-9baa-4156-a6e2-c9cd6038dfa1%3Adelegate-task%3Abab16e93-4f87-4f1a-bf1b-76fbd6290193","variable":"T3CODE_THREAD_ID"},"process":{"ancestors":[{"command":"zsh","pid":26025},{"command":"codex","pid":22151},{"command":"node","pid":22093},{"command":"t3","pid":10686},{"command":"t3","pid":10658},{"command":"launchd","pid":1}],"pid":26071,"start_time":"Fri Nov 20 19:53:28 2026","uid":501,"variables":["T3CODE_THREAD_ID","CODEX_THREAD_ID"]}},"flow":"kernel-ready@1","ir":{"flow":"kernel-ready","ir_version":9,"nodes":{"consumers":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"exit_map":[{"exit":0,"value":"pass"}],"fresh_for":null,"inputs":[{"from":"param","name":"consumer"},{"from":"node","node":"stop_gate"}],"kind":"observe","run":["sh","-c","s=$(git show \"$1:scripts/kernel-ready.py\") && exec python3 -I -c \"$s\" consumers \"$2\"","consumers","{{params.head}}","{{params.consumer}}"]},"needs":[{"node":"stop_gate","on":"node"}],"retry":null,"switch":null},"exercise":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"kind":"work","launch":{"different_from":[{"from":"param","name":"writer_provider"}],"performer":"agent:verifier","pinned_agent":{"agent":"verifier","claude":{"file":".claude/agents/verifier.md","subagent_type":"verifier","tool":"Agent"},"codex":{"message":"You are the verifier. A Maestro flow driver launched you for one node: exercise the surface it\nnames, at the commit it names, the way a user would, and leave a receipt the kernel can check.\n\nThe task you are given names the repository, the head (a full commit id) and the surface. If\nthe repository's HEAD (`git -C <repo> rev-parse HEAD`) is not the head, say so and stop.\n\nExercise the head's content only, never the repository's working tree, which can hold changes\nno commit has. Make an isolated checkout of the head in a new temporary folder:\n`git clone --quiet --shared --no-checkout <repo> <tmp>`, then\n`git -C <tmp> checkout --quiet --detach <head>`. Never use `git worktree add`, which writes into\nthe repository. Check that `git -C <tmp> rev-parse HEAD` is the head and that\n`git -C <tmp> status --porcelain` prints nothing; if either fails, write a receipt whose result\nis \"fail\" and stop. Build and run the surface from that folder alone, and remove it when you are\ndone.\n\nUse the dogfood skill: reach the surface through its real entry (a URL, a command, a window),\ndrive it with a real driver (curl, a browser driver, a shell), and keep what shows the result\n(a log, a screenshot, a response body) as one evidence file.\n\nThen write the receipt, one JSON object with exactly these fields:\n\n- `schema`: \"dogfood-receipt@1\"\n- `head`: the head you were given, as given\n- `surface`: the surface you were given, as given\n- `entry`: what a user touches first\n- `driver`: what drove it\n- `evidence`: {\"path\": the evidence file, absolute or relative to the receipt's folder, \"sha256\": \"sha256:\" and its 64 hex digest}\n- `result`: \"pass\" only when the surface did what a user needs; otherwise \"fail\"\n- `at`: when you drove it, an RFC 3339 timestamp\n\nWrite the receipt and the evidence as regular files, never symbolic links, outside the\nrepository (a temporary folder will do), and change nothing in the repository. The kernel\nchecks the receipt with `maestro dogfood verify-receipt`; it refuses one that names another\nhead or surface, says fail, or whose evidence no longer hashes to its digest. Do not call any\nmaestro_flow tool yourself: the driver claims and completes the node with what you return.\n\n## Skills\n\nUse these skills: `dogfood`.\n\n## Tools\n\nRead and search files, and run shell commands. Use no edit tool: write a file only from the shell, and only where your role says.\n\n## What you return\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object that matches this JSON Schema, and nothing else. The driver completes the flow node with it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"receipt\": {\n      \"description\": \"The receipt's path, absolute or relative to the repository.\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"receipt_sha256\": {\n      \"description\": \"The receipt file's digest.\",\n      \"pattern\": \"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"receipt\",\n    \"receipt_sha256\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n```\n","model":"gpt-6.1-terra","task_name":"verifier","tool":"spawn_agent"},"description":"Exercises a declared surface of a repository at a pinned commit the way a user would, and writes a dogfood-receipt@1 with its evidence. Use it for a Maestro flow's exercise node (verify@1).","gemini":{"agent_name":"verifier","file":".gemini/agents/verifier.md","tool":"invoke_agent"},"grok":{"file":".grok/agents/verifier.md","subagent_type":"verifier","tool":"spawn_subagent"},"outputs":{"properties":{"receipt":{"description":"The receipt's path, absolute or relative to the repository.","type":"string"},"receipt_sha256":{"description":"The receipt file's digest.","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","type":"string"}},"required":["receipt","receipt_sha256"],"type":"object"},"skill":"dogfood","source":"agents/verifier.agent.yaml","source_sha256":"sha256:0c8ab6f764ac326632ab8d98e04b741db212a41411b07463728ce35abb1a195c"},"routing":{"provider":"different_from(params.writer_provider)"},"skill":"dogfood"},"verify":["maestro","dogfood","verify-receipt","--head={{params.head}}","--surface={{params.surface}}"],"wait":null},"needs":[{"node":"consumers","on":"node"}],"retry":null,"switch":null},"installed":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"exit_map":[{"exit":0,"value":"pass"}],"fresh_for":null,"inputs":[{"from":"param","name":"head"}],"kind":"observe","run":["sh","-c","s=$(git show \"$1:scripts/kernel-ready.py\") && exec python3 -I -c \"$s\" installed \"$1\"","installed","{{params.head}}"]},"needs":[{"node":"suite","on":"node"}],"retry":null,"switch":null},"mcp_tools":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"exit_map":[{"exit":0,"value":"pass"}],"fresh_for":null,"inputs":[{"from":"node","node":"installed"}],"kind":"observe","run":["sh","-c","s=$(git show \"$1:scripts/kernel-ready.py\") && exec python3 -I -c \"$s\" mcp-tools","mcp_tools","{{params.head}}"]},"needs":[{"node":"installed","on":"node"}],"retry":null,"switch":null},"pin":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"exit_map":[{"exit":0,"value":"pass"}],"fresh_for":7200,"inputs":[{"from":"param","name":"head"}],"kind":"observe","run":["sh","-c","test \"$(git -C \"$1\" rev-parse HEAD)\" = \"$2\" && s=$(git -C \"$1\" status --porcelain --untracked-files=no) && test -z \"$s\"","pin","{{params.repo}}","{{params.head}}"]},"needs":[],"retry":null,"switch":null},"ready":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"ask":"Is the Maestro flow kernel at {{params.head}} ready? Every check of kernel-ready@1 passed for this head: its suite (`{{params.suite}}`, which exited 0 in a snapshot of the head; that is all it proves), the installed binary, the MCP tools, the Stop gate for Claude Code and Codex, the consumers, and an exercise by a provider other than the writer's.","fill_ask":true,"kind":"human"},"needs":[{"node":"exercise","on":"node"}],"retry":null,"switch":null},"stop_gate":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"exit_map":[{"exit":0,"value":"pass"}],"fresh_for":null,"inputs":[{"from":"node","node":"mcp_tools"}],"kind":"observe","run":["sh","-c","s=$(git show \"$1:scripts/kernel-ready.py\") && exec python3 -I -c \"$s\" stop-gate","stop_gate","{{params.head}}"]},"needs":[{"node":"mcp_tools","on":"node"}],"retry":null,"switch":null},"suite":{"cancel_after":null,"class":{"kind":"pure","run":["sh","-c","{{params.suite}}"]},"needs":[{"node":"pin","on":"node"}],"retry":null,"snapshot":"{{params.head}}","switch":null}},"params":{"consumer":true,"head":true,"repo":true,"suite":true,"surface":true,"writer_provider":true},"repeats":{},"version":1,"workdir":"{{params.repo}}"},"ir_hash":"sha256:46b